                "entry_id": "682f56b4-4eaf-3b9e-b4b0-da088d3ed356",
                "word": "janglery",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bb6a6a5f-e353-3e72-8382-a387b5e1c481",
                        "entry_id": "682f56b4-4eaf-3b9e-b4b0-da088d3ed356",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Chatter; gossip."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "dated",
                            "rare",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ed33e542-d818-45f9-a3df-98b1cd8d234a",
                                "sense_id": "bb6a6a5f-e353-3e72-8382-a387b5e1c481",
                                "text": "See there be no entrance into princes' courts, either of drunkenneſs, ill-ſpeaking, babling indiſcreetly, flattery, janglery, buffoonery, and ſuch other vices, which ſoil and ſhame the reputation of men."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "47cf0c25-1f83-4247-8fb9-39b4b0ff6f12",
                                "sense_id": "bb6a6a5f-e353-3e72-8382-a387b5e1c481",
                                "text": "For it is written, the janglery of women ne can nothing hide, save that which they wot not."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ae77b5e7-9c84-4a3a-ad4b-9d0519d34842",
                                "sense_id": "bb6a6a5f-e353-3e72-8382-a387b5e1c481",
                                "text": "S. Gregory saith in his dialogues that there was a nun Sabina which held her continent of her flesh, but she eschewed not the janglery of her tongue [.]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "dfe5c2d6-eacf-4322-b1db-00768a273314",
                                "sense_id": "bb6a6a5f-e353-3e72-8382-a387b5e1c481",
                                "text": "“Yes, I think. He doesn’t hold by Lancaster now, at all events. Ask Thomas! He knows all the scullions’ janglery!”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "107c0e71-56b0-4d69-b7be-3a7d01509b23",
                                "sense_id": "bb6a6a5f-e353-3e72-8382-a387b5e1c481",
                                "text": "And by this way of behaving, you shall not be put in their janglery and talking and will not have blame or defame of the world."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fd00ca3d-63dc-491e-843a-471e85ee2758",
                                "sense_id": "bb6a6a5f-e353-3e72-8382-a387b5e1c481",
                                "text": "‘Nonsense!’ he shouted. ‘I never heard such folly! You are the elder, ’tis your right to be first, foolish one. Do not prate such janglery to me, my Lord Earl of Warwick!’"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
